{"subjectId":"c","id":"modern-c","title":"C99, C11, C17 & C23 Features","group":"Standard Library, Modern C & Interview","order":56,"html":"<p class=\"lead\">Modern C is much nicer than the C89 many tutorials still teach. Use <code>-std=c17</code> (or <code>-std=c23</code>) and these features freely.</p>\n<section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-number-9\"></i>C99</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"c\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>C</figcaption><pre><code>#include &lt;stdio.h&gt;\n#include &lt;stdbool.h&gt;\n#include &lt;stdint.h&gt;\n\nstruct Point { int x, y; };\n\nstatic inline int sq(int v) { return v * v; }        /* inline functions */\n\nint main(void) {\n    // line comments\n    for (int i = 0; i &lt; 1; i++) { }                   /* declarations in for */\n    bool ready = true;                                 /* &lt;stdbool.h&gt; */\n    int64_t big = 1LL &lt;&lt; 40;                           /* &lt;stdint.h&gt;, long long */\n    struct Point p = {.y = 2, .x = 1};                 /* designated initializers */\n    int arr[5] = {[4] = 9};\n    int n = 3;\n    int vla[n];                                        /* variable-length array */\n    vla[0] = sq(n);\n    struct Point *q = &amp;(struct Point){5, 6};           /* compound literal */\n    printf(\"%d %lld %d %d %d %d %d\\n\", ready, (long long)big, p.x, arr[4], vla[0], q-&gt;y, __func__[0]);\n    return 0;\n}</code></pre></figure><figure data-lang=\"text\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption><pre><code>1 1099511627776 1 9 9 6 109</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-number-11\"></i>C11</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"c\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>C</figcaption><pre><code>#include &lt;stdio.h&gt;\n#include &lt;stdalign.h&gt;\n#include &lt;stdnoreturn.h&gt;\n#include &lt;stdlib.h&gt;\n\n/* _Generic: compile-time dispatch on the type of an expression */\n#define type_name(x) _Generic((x), \\\n    int: \"int\", double: \"double\", char *: \"char *\", default: \"other\")\n\n#define print_any(x) _Generic((x), int: print_int, double: print_double)(x)\nvoid print_int(int v) { printf(\"int %d\\n\", v); }\nvoid print_double(double v) { printf(\"double %.2f\\n\", v); }\n\n_Static_assert(sizeof(int) &gt;= 4, \"need 32-bit int\");   /* compile-time check */\n\nstruct Packet {\n    int kind;\n    union { int code; float value; };                    /* anonymous union */\n};\n\nnoreturn void die(const char *msg) { fprintf(stderr, \"%s\\n\", msg); exit(1); }\n\nint main(void) {\n    char *s = \"hi\";\n    printf(\"%s %s %s %s\\n\", type_name(42), type_name(3.0), type_name(s), type_name(1L));\n    print_any(7);\n    print_any(2.5);\n    struct Packet pk = {.kind = 1, .code = 404};\n    printf(\"%d %zu\\n\", pk.code, alignof(double));\n    if (pk.code != 404) die(\"unexpected\");\n    return 0;\n}</code></pre></figure><figure data-lang=\"text\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption><pre><code>int double char * other\nint 7\ndouble 2.50\n404 8</code></pre></figure>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr><th>C11 feature</th><th>Purpose</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>_Generic</code></td><td>Type-generic macros (how <code>&lt;tgmath.h&gt;</code> works)</td></tr><tr><td><code>_Static_assert</code> / <code>static_assert</code></td><td>Compile-time assertions</td></tr><tr><td><code>_Alignas</code> / <code>_Alignof</code></td><td>Control / query alignment</td></tr><tr><td><code>_Noreturn</code></td><td>Function never returns (<code>exit</code>, <code>abort</code>)</td></tr><tr><td>Anonymous structs/unions</td><td>Access nested members directly</td></tr><tr><td><code>_Atomic</code>, <code>&lt;stdatomic.h&gt;</code>, memory model</td><td>Portable concurrency</td></tr><tr><td><code>&lt;threads.h&gt;</code> (optional)</td><td>Threads, mutexes, condition variables</td></tr><tr><td><code>_Thread_local</code></td><td>Thread-local storage</td></tr><tr><td>Bounds-checked <code>_s</code> functions (Annex K)</td><td>Optional; rarely implemented</td></tr><tr><td><code>gets</code> removed</td><td>Finally</td></tr><tr><td><code>aligned_alloc</code>, <code>quick_exit</code>, <code>timespec_get</code></td><td>Library additions</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-number-17-small\"></i>C17</h3>\n<p>C17 (also called C18) is a <em>bug-fix</em> release: no new features, only clarifications and defect fixes to C11. <code>__STDC_VERSION__</code> is <code>201710L</code>. It is the default of GCC 8+ and recent Clang.</p>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-number-23-small\"></i>C23</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"c\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>C — compiled with -std=c23</figcaption><pre><code>#include &lt;stdio.h&gt;\n#include &lt;stdckdint.h&gt;\n\n[[nodiscard]] int twice(int x) { return 2 * x; }     /* standard attributes */\n\nenum Small : unsigned char { A, B, C };                  /* fixed underlying type */\n\nint main(void) {\n    constexpr int size = 4;                              /* true compile-time constant */\n    int arr[size] = {};                                  /* empty initializer = zero */\n    bool ok = true;                                      /* bool/true/false are keywords */\n    int *p = nullptr;                                    /* typed null pointer constant */\n    typeof(size) mask = 0b1111'0000;                     /* typeof, binary literal, digit separator */\n    auto ratio = 2.5;                                    /* type inference */\n    int sum;\n    bool overflow = ckd_add(&amp;sum, 2147483647, 1);        /* checked arithmetic */\n    static_assert(sizeof(enum Small) == 1);              /* message optional */\n    printf(\"%d %d %d %d %.1f %d %d\\n\", arr[3], ok, p == nullptr, mask, ratio, twice(size), overflow);\n    return 0;\n}</code></pre></figure><figure data-lang=\"text\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption><pre><code>0 1 1 240 2.5 8 1</code></pre></figure>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr><th>C23 feature</th><th>Replaces</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>bool</code>, <code>true</code>, <code>false</code>, <code>static_assert</code>, <code>alignas</code>… as keywords</td><td><code>&lt;stdbool.h&gt;</code> etc.</td></tr><tr><td><code>nullptr</code> / <code>nullptr_t</code></td><td><code>NULL</code> (which may be <code>0</code>)</td></tr><tr><td><code>constexpr</code> objects</td><td><code>#define</code> / <code>enum</code> constants</td></tr><tr><td><code>typeof</code>, <code>typeof_unqual</code></td><td>GNU <code>__typeof__</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>auto</code> type inference</td><td>Spelling out types</td></tr><tr><td><code>[[nodiscard]]</code>, <code>[[maybe_unused]]</code>, <code>[[deprecated]]</code>, <code>[[fallthrough]]</code></td><td><code>__attribute__</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>0b</code> literals, <code>'</code> digit separators</td><td>Hex masks</td></tr><tr><td><code>&lt;stdckdint.h&gt;</code>: <code>ckd_add</code>, <code>ckd_sub</code>, <code>ckd_mul</code></td><td>Hand-written overflow checks</td></tr><tr><td><code>#embed</code>, <code>#elifdef</code>, <code>__has_include</code></td><td>External tools, nested <code>#ifdef</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>f(void)</code> ≡ <code>f()</code>; K&amp;R definitions removed</td><td>Unprototyped functions</td></tr><tr><td>Two’s complement mandatory</td><td>Implementation-defined representations</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<details class=\"qa\"><summary>What is _Generic used for?</summary><div><p>Selecting an expression at compile time based on the type of a controlling expression — the foundation of type-generic macros like <code>&lt;tgmath.h&gt;</code>’s <code>sqrt</code> that call <code>sqrtf</code>, <code>sqrt</code> or <code>sqrtl</code> depending on the argument type. It gives C a limited form of overloading.</p></div></details>\n<details class=\"qa\"><summary>What are designated initializers?</summary><div><p>C99 syntax to initialise specific members or indexes by name: <code>struct Point p = {.y = 2, .x = 1};</code>, <code>int a[10] = {[9] = 1};</code>. Unmentioned members are zero-initialised, the order doesn’t matter, and the code survives reordering of struct fields.</p></div></details></section>"}